=== (A) ADJUDICATION of the three Q12 harvests ===

  A-1  Entry A, flagged strengthening 'any edge B_p-B_q gives a 4-cycle':
       CONFIRMED (p,h,c,q is a 4-cycle: p~h, h~c, c~q, q~p).
       explicit: p-h-c-q-p on 4 vertices, C4-free=False
       => adopted as owner's Lemma G25(a) with the owner's own proof;
          it strengthens the brief's own F7(c) (which said 'at most one').

  A-2  Entry A, Case I step 'every D-vertex has one parent on each side and
       injects into B_p x B_q, so |D| <= 9':  REFUTED as stated.
       witness small n=5: u=2, B_p=[0], B_q=[], y=4 in D has ONE parent
       (injectivity is available only on the two-parent set D2 = G24(d);
        the summary's |D| <= 9 and 'hub excess <= |D|-1' do not follow from
        the facts supplied.  Conclusion right, delivered proof NOT adopted.)

  A-3  Entry B is built on the F9 / G24(e') trigger (a hub of degree >= 6
       inside B_p u B_q).  That trigger is VACUOUS: by G25(a) N(h) & B_q = 0,
       so by G25(d)+G22 every D-child of such an h has no B_q-parent, and
       then G25(c) forces |B_q| = 0, killed by G24(b).  Entry B is therefore
       superseded, not adopted (its case analysis is unverifiable anyway:
       the artifact is a summary, not a transcript).

  A-4  Entry C's accounting device ('every addition leaves S = sum(a-3)
       unchanged or decreases it') is REFUTED as a general C4-free principle:
       HS     n=50   C4-free=True l=7.000 S=sum(a-3)=+200  (induced P6 present=True)
       ER_5   n=31   C4-free=True l=3.871 S=sum(a-3)=+27  (induced P6 present=True)
       ER_7   n=57   C4-free=True l=4.912 S=sum(a-3)=+109  (induced P6 present=True)
       A single hub with a(h)=5 contributes +2 to S; the claim can only hold
       through branch-specific structure, which the artifact does not exhibit
       (it also never treats the three unbounded-degree slots the brief named,
        and its 'maximum' witness Z u {v3,v4} has 8 vertices, below n >= 14).
